<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>P({-3},\,{-1},\,{3})</m> and <m>Q({-4},\,{-3},\,k)</m>. The distance <m>PQ</m> is <m>{3}</m>.</p><p>Find the two possible values of <m>k</m>.</p><div><m>k =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/>  or <m>k =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/> </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><m>\overrightarrow{PQ} = \begin{pmatrix} {-1} \\ {-2} \\ {k-3} \end{pmatrix}</m>, so <m>({-1})^2 + ({-2})^2 + ({k-3})^2 = {3}^2</m>.</p><p>Then <m>({k-3})^2 = {9} - {5} = {4}</m>, so <m>{k-3} = \pm {2}</m>, giving <m>k = {5}</m> or <m>k = {1}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>5</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>